        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_caption" value="Figure 1. Overall architecture of the proposed EfficientNetB4-FSDA model for garlic disease classification. The input RGB image is first encoded by an EfficientNetB4 backbone to extract deep feature representations. These features are further refined by the proposed Frequency-Spatial Dual Attention (FSDA) block. Finally, global average pooling and fully connected layers are used to predict disease categories via a softmax classifier." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=15;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
