        <mxCell id="p2_caption" value="Figure 2. Detailed structure of the proposed Frequency-Spatial Dual Attention (FSDA) block. The input feature map is processed in parallel by a frequency-channel attention branch and a CBAM-style spatial attention branch. The frequency branch models channel importance from the frequency-domain response, while the spatial branch highlights lesion-relevant regions. Their outputs are fused by element-wise addition and normalized to generate the final attention-enhanced feature map." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=14;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="21">
